{
 "about": "Reference cases for Engine's FMovingBrushTracker (notes.md). Run: node .work/tracker/run.mjs [.work/tracker/cases.json] [id ...]. Each step's full oracle output (every added/changed/removed node, surf, point, vector and vert as bit patterns, the tracker's own state and each mover's SavedPos/SavedRot/MoverLink chain) is written to results/<id>.json; results/summary.json holds per-step counts and a 16-hex digest of each step's output. Position specs: {key:k} = BasePos+KeyPos[k], BaseRot+KeyRot[k]; {from,to,alpha} = float32 key interpolation (rotation rounded); {offset:[dx,dy,dz]} added to the placed Location; {hidden:true} sets bHidden. 'frame' = Update(Actor) for every listed non-hidden mover in Level.Actors order (URender::SetupDynamics); 'update' = one Update(actor) (actor null = Update(NULL)). Control words: construct 0x037f unless noted (game-thread precision at LoadMap, not measured), Update 0x007f (inside DrawWorld, PC24). Other keys: 'movers' limits Level.Actors to those movers (map order); 'fillers' prepends a null slot, an actor without a Brush and/or a static brush; 'brief' steps report counts plus a SHA-256 of the full report; {'op':'cycle', mover, count, positions} expands to count brief frames cycling through positions. Coverage of the tracker's basic blocks over all results: coverage.txt (blocks.py).",
